#* {{quote-book |en |title=The Historical Magazine, and Notes and Queries Concerning the Antiquities, History and Biography of America |volume=VII |issue=8 |year=1863 |month=August |publisher=New York: Charles B. Richardson,{{nb...|594 & 596 Broadway}}. London: [[w:Routledge|Trübner & Co.]] |page=245 |column=2 |text=In the olden time the currency, you know, was a&nbsp;l{{sic}} in gold and silver, '''joes''', half-'''joes''' (Johannes), pistoles, moidores, doubloons, pistareens, ninepences ({{frac|12|1|2}} cents), and fourpence-half-pennies ({{frac|6|1|4}} cents) or “fippenny-bits.”}}

